<title>FRANCE: Labour union pleased with Renault ruling.</title>
<headline>Labour union pleased with Renault ruling.</headline>
<dateline>VERSAILLES, France 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A representative of the labour unions of the Belgian Vilvoorde plant of Renault SA said on Wednesday he was pleased with a Court of Appeal ruling that the carmaker could not go ahead with a closure plan before it had called a special meeting of its European works council.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the best ruling we could have got. Renault has to start all over again with the procedure. The date of July 31 does not exist anymore,&quot; said Georges Jacquemin of the CSC christian labour union.</p>
<p>Lawyers for Renault have not yet reacted to the decision.</p>
</text>
